<GuideLayout 
  title="Zero Defect Policy: How FITCLO Maintains 99% Product Consistency for Global Brands"
  type="QC"
  date="July 1, 2026"
  readTime="11 min read"
>
  <p>Scaling a fitness brand from 100 to 10,000 units requires more than just machines—it requires a culture of quality. At FITCLO, our "Zero Defect" policy is built into the fabric of our operation.</p>
  
  <h2>Multi-Stage Inspection</h2>
  <p>Quality control doesn't happen at the end; it happens at every station. We implement <strong>In-line Inspection</strong> during sewing to catch errors before the garment is finished. This is followed by a final <strong>100% Manual Inspection</strong> where every seam, thread, and logo is checked under professional lighting.</p>
  
  <h2>Fabric Stress Testing</h2>
  <p>Before cutting begins, every roll of fabric undergoes shrinkage and colorfastness testing. This ensures that the beautiful "Pantone 3405 C" green you approved doesn't fade or shrink after the customer's first wash.</p>
  
  <p>For distributors and sourcing managers, this rigor translates to fewer returns, higher customer satisfaction, and a stronger brand reputation.</p>
</GuideLayout>
